From cbbeaaf9ad12b20f2710a775d55f422e01fc2866 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:12:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] select: unit: vh and vw were swapped in px_per_unit

css_unit__px_per_unit() answered the viewport WIDTH for 1vh and the
HEIGHT for 1vw. Its callers -- css_unit_len2css_px() and so the calc()
evaluator -- then resolved `calc(100vh - 50px)` against the width: 750px
in an 800x600 viewport where it is 550. Lengths outside calc() go
through css_unit__absolute_len2pt(), which has them the right way round,
so only calc() showed it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
---
 src/select/unit.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/select/unit.c b/src/select/unit.c
index 75c33db..3cd3eed 100644
--- a/src/select/unit.c
+++ b/src/select/unit.c
@@ -267,10 +267,10 @@ static inline css_fixed css_unit__px_per_unit(
 				viewport_width);
 
 	case CSS_UNIT_VH:
-		return FDIV(viewport_width, F_100);
+		return FDIV(viewport_height, F_100);
 
 	case CSS_UNIT_VW:
-		return FDIV(viewport_height, F_100);
+		return FDIV(viewport_width, F_100);
 
 	default:
 		return 0;
-- 
